A :BEGININLINECODE block holding text that is not SSL: an SQL statement,
prose, and an HTML fragment, each ending in ';'. Inline-code bodies are
SSL read by GetInlineCode() and are analyzed and formatted as code, so a
foreign-language body is user error; the scenario records the findings
and holds the invariants on text the lexer was never meant to read.
-- input.ssl --
:BEGININLINECODE Notes;
SELECT * FROM LabSamples WHERE Status = 'P';
Hello world, this is prose;
<b>bold</b>;
:ENDINLINECODE;
-- format --
:BEGININLINECODE Notes;
	SELECT * FROM LabSamples WHERE Status = 'P';
	Hello world, this is prose;
	< b > bold < / b >;
:ENDINLINECODE;
-- diagnostics --
2:15-2:25 error unexpected_token: Unexpected identifier 'LabSamples' - expected an operator or ';'
3:7-3:12 error unexpected_token: Unexpected identifier 'world' - expected an operator or ';'
4:1-4:2 error unexpected_token: Unexpected operator '<' - expected a statement
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
2:15-2:25 error unexpected_token: Unexpected identifier 'LabSamples' - expected an operator or ';'
2:39-2:40 info equals_vs_strict_equals: For strings, '=' does prefix matching. Use '==' for exact string comparisons
3:7-3:12 error unexpected_token: Unexpected identifier 'world' - expected an operator or ';'
4:1-4:2 error unexpected_token: Unexpected operator '<' - expected a statement
